### Page 1 of 3

```text
RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
January 10, 2011
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met in regular session on this date
beginning at 6:00 p.m. in Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen;
COUNCIL MEMBERS - Mr. Allen, Ms. Ash, Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Mr. Collins, Dr. Rinne,
Mr. Pierson, Mr. Spiker and Mr. Valdez.  Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr,
City Treasurer, and Erik Rasmussen, Deputy City Attorney.  The pledge of allegiance was
recited.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to
be routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no
separate discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and
support by two other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be
considered in its normal sequence on the agenda.)  Mr. Collins moved to approve Consent
Agenda items, seconded by Mr. Spiker.  Motion carried. Voting “yes” – all members of the
governing body.
[CA]
Minutes from Regular Meeting of the Governing Body on December 22, 2010.  Motion
(per Consent Agenda) carried.
[CA]
Minutes from Sine Die Session of the Governing Body on January 3, 2011.  Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried.
[CA]
Minutes from the First Regular Meeting of the Governing Body on January 3, 2011.
Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
[CA]
Minutes from Vouchers Meeting of the Governing Body on January 4, 2011.  Motion
(per Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Valdez moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr.
Brown. Upon inquiry regarding a voucher payable for ice slicer products utilized by Street and
Alley, Jim Elias, Public Works Director, provided information on staff testing of other types of
ice melting products. Upon further inquiry regarding a voucher payable to Labor Ready for
temporary sanitation workers,  Mayor Kaysen advised he recently received a staffing analysis
from Mr. Elias and is in the process of reviewing the information. Mr. Elias stated copies of the
analysis would be provided to Council members.  Pursuant to comment on vouchers payable to
Sapp Brothers Service Center and Agland for tires and the volume of tires purchased for Fleet
vehicles, Mr. Elias responded that he would provide information to the governing body on the
annual cost incurred for tires.  Upon query, Ms. Dorr reviewed a voucher payable to Jim
Wollenburg ($648.80), for art work sales, minus payment of sales tax and other charges, relating
to a recent National Arts Program event at the Civic Center.  Motion carried. Voting “yes” – all
members of the governing body.
```

