### Page 3 of 3

```text
[CA]
Consideration of Bid #R-17-11 for furnishing one new Demo Fire Truck and Small
Equipment for the City of Cheyenne Fire & Rescue Department (1% Specific Purpose Sales &
Use Tax) -- referred to Finance Committee.
[CA]
Consideration of Bid #R-16-11 for furnishing two new packer trucks for the Sanitation
Division (Solid Waste Equipment Lease/Purchase fund) -- referred to Finance Committee.

Announcement was made that due to the Martin Luther King, Jr. holiday on Monday, Jan.
17, 2011, the following City Council meetings will instead be held on Tuesday, Jan. 18, 2011 in
the Municipal Building, 2101 O’Neil Avenue: Finance Committee will meet at 11:00 a.m. and
Public Services will meet at 12:15 p.m. in Council Meeting Room 122; Vouchers meeting will be
held at Noon in Council Chambers.
Announcement was made of the Appointment of Timothy Morton to the Greenway
Advisory Committee; and Betsy Putnam to the Laramie County Juvenile Services Joint Powers
Board, to be confirmed January 24, 2011.
Announcement was made of the Reappointment of Leda Pojman to the Housing and
Community Development Advisory Council, to be confirmed January 24, 2011.
Under other City business, John Palmer expressed his concerns with the public
participation format utilized at City Council meetings, and requested Council members consider
changing the process.  Mayor Kaysen reviewed the governing body and City Council standing
committees’ meeting process relative to opportunity for public input on agenda items.
Comments followed on current and past public participation formats.
There being no further business to come before the governing body, Mayor Kaysen
adjourned the meeting at 6:18 p.m.
Submitted by,
Carol Intlekofer, MMC
City Clerk
This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request.
Published:
Wyoming Tribune-Eagle
January 18, 2010
```
